{"name":"Good Luck Charm","hex":"#86c994","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"good","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person or an animal:\nActing in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral.","Acting in the interest of what is beneficial, ethical, or moral."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good"},{"term":"luck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that happens to someone by chance, a chance occurrence.","A favourable chance occurrence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To find something through good fortune; used with into, on, onto or upon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luck"},{"term":"charm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object, act or words believed to have magic power (usually carries a positive connotation).","The ability to persuade, delight or arouse admiration."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seduce, persuade or fascinate someone or something.","To use a magical charm upon; to subdue, control, or summon by incantation or supernatural influence; to ensorcel or exert a magical effect on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Good Luck Charm","blocks":[{"text":"\"Good Luck Charm\" is a song recorded by Elvis Presley and published by Gladys Music, Elvis Presley's publishing company, that reached number 1 on the Billboard Hot 100 list in the week ending April 21, 1962. It remained at the top of the list for two weeks. It was also No. 1 on the Cash Box chart in the US. It reached number 1 in the UK Singles Chart in the week ending May 24, 1962, and stayed there for five weeks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Elvis_Good_Luck_Charm_PS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Luck_Charm","wikidata":"Q5582744"},{"title":"Good Luck Charm (Jagged Edge song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Good Luck Charm\" is the second single from Jagged Edge's self-titled fifth album Jagged Edge. It was certified gold by the RIAA."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Good_Luck_Charm_Jagged_Edge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Luck_Charm_(Jagged_Edge_song)","wikidata":"Q5582741"},{"title":"List of lucky symbols","blocks":[{"text":"A good luck charm is an amulet or other item that is believed to bring good luck. Almost any object can be used as a charm. Coins, horseshoes and buttons are examples, as are small objects given as gifts, due to the favorable associations they make. Many souvenir shops have a range of tiny items that may be used as good luck charms. Good luck charms are often worn on the body, but not necessarily."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_lucky_symbols","wikidata":"Q1532771"},{"title":"Luck","blocks":[{"text":"Luck is a phenomenon or belief that humans may associate with experiencing improbable events, especially improbably positive or negative events.\nPhilosophical naturalism, eschewing any supernatural explanations, might suggest that positive or negative events may happen at any time, and that even improbable events can happen by random chance.\nIn this view, the epithet \"lucky\" or \"unlucky\" is a descriptive label that refers to an event's positivity, negativity, or improbability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Four-leaf_clover.jpg/330px-Four-leaf_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luck","wikidata":"Q1970348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Keychain_with_four-leaf_clover.jpg/500px-Keychain_with_four-leaf_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.